email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[non-codebase] Final delivery evidence\n\n- Gerrit change 2624 is MERGED as 0fbbe517e36076b347165d71de16af926e4c008c.\n- Gerrit change 2627 is MERGED as ee2c54f881d6ee117cbb435ce223a773a73c6d9c (submitted 2026-09-04 18:02:18 UTC); both gerrit/main and origin/main contain that commit.\n- Change 2627 received LLM-Review +1 from rebar review bot at 2026-09-04 17:46:57 UTC and Verified +1 from rebar CI bot at 2026-09-04 18:01:27 UTC.\n- Gerrit's current-revision comments endpoint returned zero unresolved comments before Submit.\n- GitHub Verified run 33901729127 completed successfully (2026-09-04 17:39:20–18:01:30 UTC), with no failed jobs and no retries.\n- Local verification on the merged-base patch: 55 focused tests passed; docs index, make lint, git diff --check, and rebar verify-commit-ticket passed.\n- Completion verification against ee2c54f881d6 produced PASS with all 15 criteria met.","timestamp":1788546448635592792}],"created_at":1788538518827650442,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d88881e9-b38b-4a46-924a-3d71daf1c6c0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3960-1016-ad4b-4c90"},{"link_uuid":"df00a118-8f47-4fd6-ae23-dcea8acc1c5a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c0d0-07b1-c699-4908"},{"link_uuid":"7abc2d86-f0b5-41cb-8d22-f847b45b0f07","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fa1d-49c0-624c-4770"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`AGENTS.md` says launch-loaded guidance must stay lean and point to maintained documentation, but its background-process section embeds a dated incident narrative, operator recovery procedure, and detector explanation. Every agent pays that context cost even when it only needs the prevention contract.\n\n## Approach\n- Replace the long `AGENTS.md` section with a compact prevention contract retaining the safety invariants, bounded-spawn and process-group cleanup example, bounded-LLM-gate exemption, and a detailed-documentation pointer.\n- Move incident evidence, detector interpretation, and operator recovery into `docs/orphaned-processes.md`; index it from `docs/README.md`.\n- Update both the module docstring and runtime report in `scripts/check_orphaned_load.py` to name `docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- Assert that flagged-process runtime output contains `docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- Preserve the commands and facts needed to prevent, detect, and reclaim orphaned processes.\n\n## Scope\n- `AGENTS.md`: compress the launch-loaded background-process rule.\n- `docs/orphaned-processes.md`: own incident evidence, prevention rationale, detector interpretation, and operator recovery.\n- `docs/README.md`: index the operations page.\n- `scripts/check_orphaned_load.py`: replace both stale `AGENTS.md` recovery pointers.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py`: protect the runtime runbook reference.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `python scripts/check_docs_index.py`.\n- Run focused documentation and orphan-detector tests.\n- Run `make lint` with the worktree virtualenv first on PATH.\n- Verify every moved invariant, command, and runbook reference remains reachable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The `AGENTS.md` background-process section contains no more than 35 physical source lines.\n- [x] The compact section includes a wall-clock-bounded spawn plus process-group cleanup example.\n- [x] The compact section states that no spawned process may reach PPID 1 and that each subagent must reap its own helpers.\n- [x] The compact section prohibits unbounded busy loops without a wall-clock bound.\n- [x] The compact section explicitly forbids applying timeouts to bounded LLM gate operations.\n- [x] Dated incident evidence is absent from `AGENTS.md` and present in `docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- [x] Orphan-detector interpretation and operator reclamation steps are absent from `AGENTS.md` and present in `docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- [x] The Operations section of `docs/README.md` links `orphaned-processes.md` as the prevention, detection, and recovery procedure.\n- [x] The detailed page documents bounded spawn, process-group cleanup, read-only detection, and confirmed reclamation commands.\n- [x] Both recovery pointers in `scripts/check_orphaned_load.py` name `docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- [x] A regression test proves flagged-process runtime output contains `docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- [x] Documentation checks and focused tests pass.\n- [x] `make lint` passes with the worktree virtualenv first on PATH.\n- [x] [non-codebase] Gerrit reports `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and no unresolved comments.\\n  provenance: environment=rebar.solutions.navateam.com-and-GitHub-Actions; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Authenticated Gerrit REST and GitHub Actions queries read the actual change, comments, labels, and CI run.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The change is submitted to `main`.\\n  provenance: environment=rebar.solutions.navateam.com; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Gerrit Submit returned MERGED and both Gerrit and GitHub main refs resolved the resulting commit.\n\n## Verification\nCount physical source lines from the background-process H2 heading through the line before the next H2; search for every preserved invariant, command, and runbook reference; run focused tests and lint; then confirm Gerrit labels and merged status before closing the ticket.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"Replace the launch-loaded orphan-process narrative with a concise prevention contract and documentation pointer."},{"path":"docs/orphaned-processes.md","reason":"Own incident evidence, prevention rationale, detector interpretation, and operator recovery."},{"path":"docs/README.md","reason":"Index the orphan-process operations page."},{"path":"scripts/check_orphaned_load.py","reason":"Point runtime recovery guidance to the canonical runbook